WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.169 --> 00:00:03.710
Right now, we're gonna look at lighting

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:04.950
with Intamin Motion.

3
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.469
Now again, we're not gonna cover in depth

4
00:00:06.469 --> 00:00:08.189
as much as we will in later courses.

5
00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:09.769
However, let's get a little bit started

6
00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:11.150
so you can get familiarized

7
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.789
and start playing around with the lighting

8
00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:14.869
to really get a good feel for it.

9
00:00:14.869 --> 00:00:17.149
And as you can imagine, lighting is very important

10
00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:19.030
because it does set up the mood

11
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:22.160
of what you're trying to convey.

12
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.199
So again, what mood are you going for?

13
00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:26.559
You need to ask yourself that before anything.

14
00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.160
If it's an outside scene

15
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.199
or a scene that's affected by the outside,

16
00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:31.800
such as our lake house,

17
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.140
you may want to see how things are affected at nighttime.

18
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.100
So you could change the time of day

19
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.060
as part of the ambiance settings.

20
00:00:41.039 --> 00:00:42.640
And it will affect the entire scene.

21
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.659
So that's what's kind of nice.

22
00:00:43.659 --> 00:00:45.759
You'll get some natural reflections on the inside,

23
00:00:45.759 --> 00:00:47.200
which can give you an idea of,

24
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.640
you know, like the color of your walls

25
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.539
or how the fabric may look differently at night

26
00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:53.460
compared to during the day.

27
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:54.960
But again, we're just gonna kind of mess around

28
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.119
with a little bit of lighting

29
00:00:56.119 --> 00:00:58.679
just so you can get an idea of what is there.

30
00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:02.530
And then we'll kind of move on from there.

31
00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:03.549
So what we're gonna do

32
00:01:03.549 --> 00:01:06.629
is we are gonna access the lights via the library,

33
00:01:06.629 --> 00:01:08.930
and we're gonna place a spotlight into the scene,

34
00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.909
one or two, or maybe even three.

35
00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:11.750
And then we can go over

36
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.629
and play around with the temperatures.

37
00:01:13.629 --> 00:01:14.750
Now there are some other ones

38
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.909
that are available to us as well.

39
00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.750
So let's go ahead and hop right back in

40
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:20.870
to our Twinmotion scene.

41
00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:22.069
And I've already got it highlighted

42
00:01:22.069 --> 00:01:25.510
on these three lights that are a little head over.

43
00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.989
And you'll see right now we do have a spotlight.

44
00:01:27.989 --> 00:01:30.390
Now you can rename it if you wish to,

45
00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.310
like you come over here

46
00:01:31.329 --> 00:01:33.930
and maybe put the left and center and right.

47
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:35.030
But right now I'm just gonna leave it

48
00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.730
to kind of keep it simple.

49
00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.290
And you'll see over here to the right,

50
00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:40.969
we do have ways to add some haze

51
00:01:40.969 --> 00:01:43.310
and different color temperatures.

52
00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.930
Now right now it is set at 4613 kelvins,

53
00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:47.170
which is a warmer temperature,

54
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:50.049
but you could cool it down and change it through here.

55
00:01:50.049 --> 00:01:51.870
And you'll see that overall effect later

56
00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.010
when we are activating our scene.

57
00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.049
But right now let's just go ahead

58
00:01:55.049 --> 00:01:56.689
and find where those lights are.

59
00:01:56.689 --> 00:01:58.370
Come over here to the library,

60
00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:01.129
look for lights, and you'll see spotlight.

61
00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:02.989
Now you may also see some neon lights,

62
00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.590
which you could put over the kitchen.

63
00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.750
You could do an omni-direction,

64
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.069
which will give you a nice overall glow,

65
00:02:08.069 --> 00:02:11.030
but you'll also notice these IES.

66
00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:14.270
These are profiles that are pretty standardized lighting.

67
00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:17.030
So a lot of the settings have already been set up for us

68
00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:19.789
so it would be more likely that we'll use these

69
00:02:19.789 --> 00:02:20.710
when you are working

70
00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.189
with more specific architectural lighting.

71
00:02:23.189 --> 00:02:26.009
So just be aware that that's what those are for.

72
00:02:26.009 --> 00:02:28.069
But we're just gonna go ahead and grab a spotlight.

73
00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:30.150
Just kind of place it wherever we want.

74
00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:31.969
I mean, you can place it anywhere that you'd like to,

75
00:02:31.969 --> 00:02:32.810
but I'm just gonna go ahead

76
00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.729
and kind of place it right there.

77
00:02:34.729 --> 00:02:36.770
And it may not be exactly where you want it,

78
00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:37.689
in which case is fine.

79
00:02:37.689 --> 00:02:40.349
You can just kind of pull that right up into there

80
00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:43.050
and kind of get in a little closer.

81
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.569
And remember, you can always snap to a surface.

82
00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:47.770
You don't want to kind of snap right in there.

83
00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:49.930
Kind of gets a little picky sometimes.

84
00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:51.930
But yeah, just get as close to the area

85
00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:54.379
that you want in that bulb.

86
00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:57.139
So we can also do a really cool thing about duplicating.

87
00:02:57.139 --> 00:02:58.819
So if you're adding a lot of lights

88
00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.919
or say multiple chairs like what's down there,

89
00:03:00.919 --> 00:03:02.960
there's multiple ways to create that.

90
00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:05.360
You could just drag and drop another one,

91
00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.159
or you could hold down your Control, Shift

92
00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:11.319
and drag this over.

93
00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:13.240
You have to kind of get that little guy there,

94
00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:17.099
but as you see, it will now create a duplicate.

95
00:03:17.099 --> 00:03:19.879
But you'll also get some options here.

96
00:03:19.879 --> 00:03:21.719
You can do it as an instance,

97
00:03:21.719 --> 00:03:23.520
in which case any changes that you make

98
00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.840
to one of the other lights,

99
00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.060
it's part of that instance,

100
00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.840
which would be just this guy.

101
00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.659
You could leave it at instance,

102
00:03:29.659 --> 00:03:31.659
or you could do it as a copy.

103
00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:33.080
Now the copy will keep it separate

104
00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:35.819
so you can change things regardless of,

105
00:03:35.819 --> 00:03:38.199
like the lighting, the cone, the temperature.

106
00:03:38.199 --> 00:03:39.259
You could do those individually.

107
00:03:39.259 --> 00:03:41.099
So if that's what you're wanting to do, great.

108
00:03:41.099 --> 00:03:42.740
But it's really great for the example

109
00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.620
of changing out chairs.

110
00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.379
For example, you'd want them instances

111
00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:48.219
because then you could change them all out.

112
00:03:48.219 --> 00:03:50.139
So if you replace the material of one,

113
00:03:50.139 --> 00:03:52.759
it replaces the material of all of the chairs.

114
00:03:52.759 --> 00:03:54.340
So just keep that in mind.

115
00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.699
I'm going to go ahead and leave it as an instance,

116
00:03:55.699 --> 00:03:57.060
and I only need one,

117
00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.879
but see you can even adjust the spacing.

118
00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:00.800
So let's say you want to have them staggered out.

119
00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:02.879
You can have multiple staggered out.

120
00:04:02.879 --> 00:04:05.280
That could be like picket fences or anything like that.

121
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:08.120
So any object that you control shift and drag

122
00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:10.580
will give you this copy option.

123
00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.159
So I'm just going to leave everything as default.

124
00:04:12.159 --> 00:04:13.939
Just go ahead and let that go.

125
00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:16.839
And we'll go ahead and change over here.

126
00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:18.920
We're going to change the color temperature.

127
00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:20.639
And you will notice that when you come over here

128
00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:21.480
to the light,

129
00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.879
it too will have the same color temperature

130
00:04:23.879 --> 00:04:25.199
because it is an instance.

131
00:04:25.259 --> 00:04:28.060
However, this one will have a different one

132
00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:30.540
and we could change this into really warm.

133
00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.379
Coming back to here,

134
00:04:31.379 --> 00:04:34.089
you'll see that these two will have the same.

135
00:04:34.089 --> 00:04:37.629
So that's the great thing about copying with an instance.

136
00:04:37.629 --> 00:04:38.970
So keep that in mind.

137
00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.449
Go ahead and go around in your scene

138
00:04:40.449 --> 00:04:41.569
and kind of play around.

139
00:04:41.569 --> 00:04:43.290
We'll put this up to five on the speed

140
00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.529
so I can zoom in on out a little quicker

141
00:04:45.529 --> 00:04:47.329
and you'll see some really great objects

142
00:04:47.329 --> 00:04:48.769
in which you can swap out

143
00:04:48.769 --> 00:04:50.889
or even change the furniture itself,

144
00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:52.290
but have some fun.

145
00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.930
That's what you want to do here.

146
00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:54.769
So let's take a look back

147
00:04:54.769 --> 00:04:57.189
into our little PowerPoint here real quick

148
00:04:57.189 --> 00:05:00.029
and you can see all the settings that are available to you

149
00:05:00.029 --> 00:05:02.990
but next we are going to explore seasons.

150
00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.430
So we can change the time of day,

151
00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:08.589
but also we can change it to snowing on the outside.

152
00:05:08.589 --> 00:05:09.629
Let's hop right in.
